930
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:27,040
He Who Pulls the Strings

931
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:33,260
It was way too easy to get in.

932
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:36,100
Their entire security's probably out 
guarding their transports.

933
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:40,620
Our target is the manager, 
an elf woman known as Luna.

934
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:41,940
Let's find her office...

935
00:03:44,170 --> 00:03:45,690
Is that...

936
00:03:46,110 --> 00:03:48,340
Thank you for coming to Mitsugoshi.

937
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:50,690
I am the manager, Luna.

938
00:03:50,690 --> 00:03:53,150
And I am here to welcome you.

939
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:56,550
What?!

940
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:01,750
But there's no sign of any bodyguard.

941
00:04:01,750 --> 00:04:03,980
Her confidence is a bluff.

942
00:04:04,210 --> 00:04:08,090
I am the man who earned the title of Leaf One, 
strongest of the Clovers.

943
00:04:08,090 --> 00:04:10,650
No one has engaged me in battle 
and come out unscathed!

944
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:15,190
If you don't wanna die, 
then be a good girl and say goodnight!

945
00:04:16,210 --> 00:04:19,480
That hurts!

946
00:04:21,990 --> 00:04:23,500
Y-You...

947
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,890
Huh?

948
00:04:24,890 --> 00:04:26,010
Ugh!

949
00:04:26,010 --> 00:04:28,900
In these situations, you start with a powerful 
frontal attack then play it by ear!

950
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:31,020
Don't you know that?

951
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:32,020
Huh?

952
00:04:32,210 --> 00:04:34,800
This is the problem with entitled customers!

953
00:04:36,290 --> 00:04:38,790
<i>That black artifact...</i>

954
00:04:38,790 --> 00:04:40,190
<i>It can't be!</i>

955
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:45,000
<i>She's fast!</i>

956
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:45,900
<i>But...</i>

957
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:51,810
Take that and that 
and that and that and that!

958
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:48,850
<i>That's all she is.</i>

959
00:04:49,090 --> 00:04:51,810
<i>She's fast, but she's a total amateur!</i>

960
00:04:51,810 --> 00:04:53,000
And that!

961
00:04:56,200 --> 00:05:00,270
That footwork! You're a student of 
the Western Liechtenroi style of fencing, aren't you?

962
00:05:00,510 --> 00:05:01,340
<i>What?</i>

963
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:03,480
<i>She identified my fighting style 
in just seconds?</i><i></i>

964
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:06,250
Now that I know how you fight, 
I can easily counter it!

965
00:05:06,250 --> 00:05:14,400
Take that and that 
and that and that and that!

966
00:05:08,410 --> 00:05:11,110
<i>She should be able to predict 
my every move now,</i>

967
00:05:11,110 --> 00:05:13,110
<i>but her approach is exactly the same!</i><i></i>

968
00:05:13,110 --> 00:05:14,400
<i>She </i>is<i> an amateur!</i><i></i>

969
00:05:17,710 --> 00:05:20,480
That hurts!

970
00:05:24,710 --> 00:05:26,790
<i>I was absolutely sure that was a direct hit!</i>

971
00:05:26,790 --> 00:05:29,400
<i>So, why? What the hell is going on?!</i><i></i>

972
00:05:30,410 --> 00:05:33,900
You are a skilled warrior 
if you managed to strike me!

973
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:35,100
Very well.

974
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:38,310
For that, I grant you 
the honor of facing my full fury!

975
00:05:42,310 --> 00:05:43,460
<i>Dammit!</i>

976
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:45,310
<i>What is with all that 
excessive magical energy?!</i>

977
00:05:45,590 --> 00:05:47,300
<i>And her battle cry!</i><i></i>

978
00:05:49,190 --> 00:05:52,100
Hear what my great lord 
and master taught me!

979
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:55,130
Lemme think...

980
00:05:55,130 --> 00:05:57,200
For you, Gamma...

981
00:05:57,200 --> 00:06:00,540
Your stats are ridiculously high, so...

982
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:02,300
To start with...

983
00:06:02,810 --> 00:06:05,270
"Jam a lot of magical energy 
into it and hack away!"

984
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:11,770
"And when you slash, 
make sure to look intimidating!"

985
00:06:11,770 --> 00:06:12,440
Take that and—

986
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:23,610
Huh?

987
00:06:26,820 --> 00:06:28,610
Well played, my good sir.

988
00:06:28,610 --> 00:06:30,940
Acting as though you were 
only evading my attack

989
00:06:30,940 --> 00:06:34,200
while using the lay of the land 
to set a clever trap.

990
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:38,540
I'd expect nothing less from 
a grand master of the Liechtenroi style.

991
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:39,940
Your nose is bleeding.

992
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:44,100
Uh, anyway, I don't want anything more 
to do with this woman—

993
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:45,210
I mean!

994
00:06:45,210 --> 00:06:49,610
Apparently, she is too much 
for me to handle.

995
00:06:49,610 --> 00:06:52,590
Men! It's time you quit messing around! 
We need to beat a tactical—

996
00:06:52,590 --> 00:06:54,210
As for your missing children...

997
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:57,300
We have been looking after them for you.

998
00:06:59,910 --> 00:07:01,800
Be careful, you two!

999
00:07:02,610 --> 00:07:05,710
That man has mastered 
the Liechtenroi technique.

1000
00:07:05,710 --> 00:07:08,670
He's most likely one of the greatest fencers 
in the entire world!

1001
00:07:08,670 --> 00:07:10,600
That is impressive.

1002
00:07:11,310 --> 00:07:14,100
No, I'm not! I'm just...

1003
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:18,600
But I have seen the secret 
behind your eminent power.

1004
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:21,410
From now on, 
I will show you my full strength!

1005
00:07:22,510 --> 00:07:24,400
<i>Please make it stop...</i>

1006
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:26,080
<i>Damn it all!</i>

1007
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:28,270
You won't get away from me!

1008
00:07:28,270 --> 00:07:29,900
Take tha—

1009
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:33,020
<i>Hup!</i>

1010
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:02,010
That was my secret technique.

1011
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:04,880
The Self-Sacrifice Spinning Wheel.

1012
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:08,380
Your nose is bleeding.

1013
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:08,380


1014
00:08:10,010 --> 00:08:12,400
The Clovers haven't returned, you say?

1015
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:20,850
Late Night Explosion at Mitsugoshi. Was It an Accident?

1016
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:20,850
Late Night Explosion at Mitsugoshi. Was It an Accident?

1017
00:08:12,810 --> 00:08:14,380
Y-Yes, sir.

1018
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:17,010
Neither have the reinforcements we sent.

1019
00:08:17,010 --> 00:08:20,500
And we even lost contact 
with the lookout team.

1020
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:26,410
Mr. Gettan, there are members of the MCA 
that have ties with Mitsugoshi.

1021
00:08:26,410 --> 00:08:27,500
I'm afraid this failure—

1022
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:31,090
I mean, this incident will 
get them talking again.

1023
00:08:31,090 --> 00:08:32,200
Then shut them up.

1024
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,710
Y-Yes, sir.

1025
00:08:41,210 --> 00:08:47,200
I should've known that naming them Clovers wouldn't make 
those sorry excuses for bandits equal to the Knights.

1026
00:08:47,750 --> 00:08:50,460
I would've liked to use 
some of the Children,

1027
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:52,690
but the Cult is running low 
on resources, as well.

1028
00:08:53,020 --> 00:08:55,380
First Zenon, then that old fossil...

1029
00:08:55,380 --> 00:08:58,020
They're both dead, 
but they're still getting in my way.

1030
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:02,980
But that is exactly why this is the perfect opportunity 
for me to demonstrate my power.

1031
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:06,750
The Major Corporate Alliance 
is nothing more than a disposable pawn.

1032
00:09:06,750 --> 00:09:10,610
I only need them to stay afloat long enough 
for me to complete my preparations.

1033
00:09:11,670 --> 00:09:13,900
Just a little while longer.

1034
00:09:15,090 --> 00:09:16,800
Soon...

1035
00:09:20,090 --> 00:09:21,720
I will have power.

1036
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:25,670
Power that no one will be able 
to take from me!

1037
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:25,670


1038
00:09:57,910 --> 00:09:58,730
Well?

1039
00:09:59,130 --> 00:10:00,670
I think you did good.

1040
00:10:00,670 --> 00:10:03,000
And you'll probably 
just keep getting better.

1041
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:04,800
Really?

1042
00:10:05,930 --> 00:10:08,510
<i>Was it a change of mindset?</i>

1043
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:11,190
<i>Or did she figure something out?</i>

1044
00:10:11,590 --> 00:10:15,090
<i>When a character suddenly gets a level up, 
it's usually one of those things.</i><i></i>

1045
00:10:15,630 --> 00:10:17,300
But it's not enough.

1046
00:10:17,900 --> 00:10:19,690
I need more power.

1047
00:10:20,130 --> 00:10:21,200
Cool...

1048
00:10:22,670 --> 00:10:24,880
Ask me why.

1049
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:25,650
Why?

1050
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:30,100
Because all I could do was watch.

1051
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:33,600
Now Rose has gone off alone.

1052
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:36,300
Oriana has lost its king.

1053
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:39,600
It's a real mess right now, and she's...

1054
00:10:41,210 --> 00:10:44,000
My friend is suffering, and I...

1055
00:10:45,110 --> 00:10:47,840
I need more power,

1056
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:50,500
and there are a lot of other things 
I'm lacking, too.

1057
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:54,310
While we lead our everyday lives, 
the world keeps moving forward in secret.

1058
00:11:00,110 --> 00:11:03,910
If I don't move with it, 
I'll be left behind.

1059
00:11:05,710 --> 00:11:08,410
I don't wanna be an outsider anymore.

1060
00:11:08,810 --> 00:11:10,300
Uh-huh...

1061
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:13,770
It's strange.

1062
00:11:14,510 --> 00:11:17,150
Since I started actively choosing 
to move forward,

1063
00:11:17,150 --> 00:11:19,840
time has started to move faster.

1064
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,410
That's just how it is.

1065
00:11:22,380 --> 00:11:24,810
Must be nice to be so carefree.

1066
00:11:29,010 --> 00:11:32,710
I sincerely hope you'll be able 
to stay that way your whole life.

1067
00:11:59,750 --> 00:12:03,150
Extra large char siu with extra veggies, 
hold the back fat and garlic.

1068
00:12:03,420 --> 00:12:04,420
Coming up.

1069
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,100
Production is complete.

1070
00:12:15,230 --> 00:12:16,410
It's time!

1071
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:22,510
Here you go.

1072
00:12:22,970 --> 00:12:22,970


1073
00:12:23,610 --> 00:12:25,590
The domain formerly ruled 
by Viscount Grease...

1074
00:12:25,590 --> 00:12:28,340
It is currently run 
by a disinterested local magistrate,

1075
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:30,440
and law enforcement is less than thorough.

1076
00:12:31,170 --> 00:12:36,100
Naturally, they wouldn't bother sparing any personnel 
to inspect the abandoned mine at the edge of the domain.

1077
00:12:36,590 --> 00:12:39,400
I am truly happy that this place 
has been brought to my attention.

1078
00:12:40,350 --> 00:12:42,600
We produce our counterfeit bills here,

1079
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:45,010
and transport them temporarily 
to the Lawless City.

1080
00:12:45,010 --> 00:12:47,410
Then, we disguise our distribution channels

1081
00:12:47,410 --> 00:12:49,810
and introduce them 
to the Royal Capital of Midgar.

1082
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:53,310
What do you think, Mr. Smith?

1083
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:56,710
For all the time we devoted 
to creating the printing plates,

1084
00:12:56,710 --> 00:12:58,900
I believe the finished product 
is quite good, don't you?

1085
00:13:00,090 --> 00:13:04,230
Of the two, can you tell 
which is the authentic bill?

1086
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:11,010
The answer goes without saying.

1087
00:13:13,310 --> 00:13:16,310
On comparison, one of them uses paper 
of slightly coarser quality.

1088
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:19,540
There are differences 
in the bleed of the ink.

1089
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:22,270
And surely I don't need to describe 
the distortions in the print?

1090
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:23,800
It's true!

1091
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:26,230
But we double- and triple-checked!

1092
00:13:26,230 --> 00:13:28,110
I don't need to bullsh—

1093
00:13:28,110 --> 00:13:30,000
point out any more than that, do I?

1094
00:13:31,290 --> 00:13:32,590
You do not.

1095
00:13:32,590 --> 00:13:34,670
Obviously the bill of lesser quality...

1096
00:13:34,670 --> 00:13:36,100
...is the real one.

1097
00:13:34,670 --> 00:13:36,100
...is the fake.

1098
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:37,100
What?

1099
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:38,200
What?

1100
00:13:43,810 --> 00:13:48,420
It appears that you perfected it to such a high degree 
that you have surpassed the authentic article.

1101
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:50,020
I had not foreseen that possibility.

1102
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,130
Shall we start over and make new ones?

1103
00:13:53,130 --> 00:13:54,540
That won't be necessary.

1104
00:13:54,950 --> 00:13:57,600
I doubt anyone other than myself 
will be able to tell the difference.

1105
00:13:57,980 --> 00:14:00,210
I am no match for your intellect, Mr. Smith.

1106
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:03,260
I was thinking we would 
begin distribution right away.

1107
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:04,420
Does that suit you?

1108
00:14:04,420 --> 00:14:05,210
Yes.

1109
00:14:06,510 --> 00:14:10,380
Once there are more bills in circulation, 
the authorities will look for the source.

1110
00:14:10,380 --> 00:14:14,500
I am counting on you, Mr. Smith, 
to handle that situation, as planned.

1111
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:21,350
But that man Gettan is mine.

1112
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:23,610
Is it revenge?

1113
00:14:25,250 --> 00:14:28,510
Gettan took everything from me.

1114
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:34,310
My mother, my friends, my entire village...

1115
00:14:35,340 --> 00:14:37,000
Now it's my turn.

1116
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:41,100
I will seize everything from him.

1117
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:43,290
I will kill him,

1118
00:14:43,290 --> 00:14:45,800
but not until after I have taken it all.

1119
00:14:50,610 --> 00:14:51,690
Have it your way.

1120
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:56,410
But take care you don't 
turn down the wrong path.

1121
00:14:58,210 --> 00:14:58,210


1122
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:02,900
Counterfeit bills?

1123
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:06,650
Yes, of the Major Corporate 
Alliance's currency.

1124
00:15:06,650 --> 00:15:09,880
We found them in several of our stores 
throughout the Royal Capital.

1125
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:14,880
Then, our decision to accept 
our competitor's bills has borne fruit.

1126
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:19,610
Although originally, that was so we could 
take credit away from their currency.

1127
00:15:20,310 --> 00:15:21,880
How much is in circulation?

1128
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:23,810
Not much yet.

1129
00:15:23,810 --> 00:15:27,290
The customers who paid with them 
are unaware the bills were counterfeit,

1130
00:15:27,290 --> 00:15:29,560
so we haven't determined 
where they infiltrated from.

1131
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:32,340
Does the Major Corporate Alliance 
know about this?

1132
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:34,670
They don't seem to have realized yet.

1133
00:15:34,670 --> 00:15:38,210
They're working to issue more bills, 
without a care in the world.

1134
00:15:38,210 --> 00:15:40,040
See to it that they do realize.

1135
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:44,010
If the citizens find out their money is counterfeit, 
we'll have a crisis on our hands.

1136
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:48,310
If anything happens to inspire doubt 
in the value of paper money,

1137
00:15:48,310 --> 00:15:50,200
it'll hurt our business, as well.

1138
00:15:50,710 --> 00:15:51,810
Hold on.

1139
00:15:52,630 --> 00:15:54,480
Was that their plan all along?

1140
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:57,310
To instigate a credit collapse?

1141
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:00,630
But that would bring about 
their own downfall.

1142
00:16:00,630 --> 00:16:02,000
Lady Alpha?

1143
00:16:02,710 --> 00:16:04,040
It's nothing.

1144
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:06,340
Find out where the counterfeit bills 
are coming from.

1145
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:08,090
That's our top priority.

1146
00:16:08,090 --> 00:16:09,320
Yes, Lady Alpha.

1147
00:16:10,910 --> 00:16:13,350
If this turns out to be more 
than a minor cash grab...

1148
00:16:14,250 --> 00:16:17,900
then who could be behind it? And why?

1149
00:16:18,590 --> 00:16:20,300
A counterfeit bill, you say?

1150
00:16:20,300 --> 00:16:21,340
Yes, sir.

1151
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:24,310
A cashier at one of our corporate stores 
found it a little while ago.

1152
00:16:30,730 --> 00:16:31,910
Which is it?

1153
00:16:31,910 --> 00:16:32,960
Sir?

1154
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:35,700
Oh, yes, of course, it was...

1155
00:16:36,110 --> 00:16:37,690
The poorly made one...

1156
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:40,400
I think, maybe?

1157
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:44,630
No matter.

1158
00:16:44,630 --> 00:16:46,100
Find out where it came from.

1159
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:48,350
Yes, sir. Right away, sir!

1160
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:55,920
The number of banknotes 
we have in circulation

1161
00:16:55,920 --> 00:17:00,020
already exceeds the total value 
of the MCA assets that give them their credit.

1162
00:17:00,710 --> 00:17:04,500
The same should be true for Mitsugoshi.

1163
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:07,090
The only thing that can guarantee 
the value of paper money

1164
00:17:07,090 --> 00:17:11,610
is the vague concept of the "credit" given to it 
by the unenlightened masses.

1165
00:17:12,020 --> 00:17:13,960
A counterfeit bill...

1166
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:16,000
A piece of paper like the banknotes,

1167
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,460
but without the guaranteed value 
promised to the real ones...

1168
00:17:18,460 --> 00:17:20,910
It is a genuine, bona fide, 
worthless scrap of paper.

1169
00:17:20,910 --> 00:17:23,210
If the world were to learn 
of their existence,

1170
00:17:23,210 --> 00:17:25,980
every citizen would 
simultaneously begin to harbor doubts.

1171
00:17:26,790 --> 00:17:29,790
They will fear that even 
the real bills in their own wallets

1172
00:17:29,790 --> 00:17:32,940
may be nothing more than paper.

1173
00:17:32,940 --> 00:17:36,590
Those offhand feelings, 
that vague ideation...

1174
00:17:36,590 --> 00:17:38,900
It'll cause the collapse of the credit 
given to paper money.

1175
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:46,000
Which is why we had been preparing 
to begin circulating our own counterfeit paper bills.

1176
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,840
By intentionally bringing about 
the downfall of credit,

1177
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:53,670
we would bankrupt the Major Corporate Alliance, 
and the abominable Mitsugoshi company with it.

1178
00:17:53,670 --> 00:17:56,790
That was the mission given to me 
by the Cult.

1179
00:17:56,790 --> 00:18:00,360
But the plan wasn't supposed 
to go into effect

1180
00:18:00,360 --> 00:18:03,500
until after we had recovered all the Cult assets 
that were hidden within the MCA.

1181
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:08,600
Those assets are mixed up in our more 
public businesses and organizations.

1182
00:18:09,130 --> 00:18:12,290
It should take time 
and effort to retrieve them.

1183
00:18:12,290 --> 00:18:15,400
Did they not understand that 
when they enacted this plan?

1184
00:18:15,810 --> 00:18:20,200
If we sit back and watch 
as the counterfeit bills go into circulation,

1185
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:24,500
the Cult could end up losing 
enormous amounts of money.

1186
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:26,630
What is this?

1187
00:18:26,630 --> 00:18:28,310
What is happening?

1188
00:18:40,910 --> 00:18:42,520
Confirming target.

1189
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:45,840
We know this train is carrying cargo 
from the Lawless City.

1190
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:49,170
And that cargo includes the counterfeit bills 
mingled with other stolen goods.

1191
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:52,000
We will let other teams search for 
the counterfeiters

1192
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,150
while we move to recover 
the bills in question.

1193
00:18:54,710 --> 00:18:57,750
Number 666, you do not make any decisions.

1194
00:18:57,750 --> 00:18:59,850
I am the leader, 
and you will follow <i>my</i> orders.

1195
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,310
I understand that.

1196
00:19:02,710 --> 00:19:05,400
No, you don't. That's why I'm reminding you.

1197
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:07,510
The last mission, the one before that...

1198
00:19:07,510 --> 00:19:10,000
What are you so panicked about?

1199
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,170
I am not panicked.

1200
00:19:12,170 --> 00:19:14,840
There you go, keeping everything bottled up.

1201
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:17,300
We can't understand you 
if you don't talk to us.

1202
00:19:17,810 --> 00:19:19,710
That's enough, you two.

1203
00:19:19,710 --> 00:19:22,060
Right now, we need to focus on the mission.

1204
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:23,170
You're right.

1205
00:19:23,170 --> 00:19:25,010
Hey, you just ate something!

1206
00:19:25,010 --> 00:19:25,910
I'm eating nothing.

1207
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:28,090
You put something in your mouth! 
I know you did!

1208
00:19:28,090 --> 00:19:29,590
We're on the job! 
You can at least wait until...

1209
00:19:43,040 --> 00:19:44,670
There aren't any passengers.

1210
00:19:44,670 --> 00:19:47,230
This train is transporting contraband,

1211
00:19:47,230 --> 00:19:49,040
so it makes sense...

1212
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:51,940
But we're not seeing any guards, either.

1213
00:19:53,770 --> 00:19:54,970
Be careful!

1214
00:20:04,830 --> 00:20:06,060
Now, then...

1215
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:09,700
Might I see your tickets?

1216
00:20:11,350 --> 00:20:12,730
Oh, please!

1217
00:20:13,190 --> 00:20:14,600
You think this will...

1218
00:20:15,610 --> 00:20:18,060
It's kinda unbreakable!

1219
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:20,910
Magically-reinforced thread?

1220
00:20:20,910 --> 00:20:21,810
Who are you?

1221
00:20:21,810 --> 00:20:23,810
John Smith.

1222
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:33,770
Putting yourself within death's reach to eliminate 
the distance between yourself and the enemy.

1223
00:20:34,210 --> 00:20:35,770
That was the correct choice.

1224
00:20:35,770 --> 00:20:36,480
However...

1225
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:40,440
You're too inexperienced 
to risk it all on a single attack.

1226
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:42,400
Number 666!

1227
00:20:42,750 --> 00:20:46,350
I knew you people would be 
the first to figure it out.

1228
00:20:46,810 --> 00:20:48,500
But it's too soon.

1229
00:20:49,820 --> 00:20:51,310
You do not need...

1230
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:53,400
to learn any more.

1231
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:54,270
Not yet!

1232
00:21:10,380 --> 00:21:11,960
Stop! I still haven't—

1233
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:13,150
Number 666!

1234
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:16,710
It's over, Number 666.

1235
00:21:16,710 --> 00:21:17,960
But...

1236
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:20,650
If we go after him without a plan, 
we'll fall into the exact same trap.

1237
00:21:21,130 --> 00:21:23,700
Surely you're smart enough 
to understand that.

1238
00:21:25,790 --> 00:21:28,600
Aw, they started speeding up.

1239
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:32,000
I don't think we can catch up now, 
even if we run.

1240
00:21:33,820 --> 00:21:36,200
We'll go back and report to Lady Gamma.

1241
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:37,250
Understood?

1242
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:39,520
Yes.

1243
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:45,980
John Smith...

1244
00:21:47,340 --> 00:21:49,010
That power...

1245
00:21:51,210 --> 00:21:52,600
Why...

1246
00:21:53,110 --> 00:21:56,020
Why am I so...

1247
00:21:57,210 --> 00:21:58,110
Why...

1248
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:01,700
Why am I so weak?

